WEBVTT

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:12.580
A small leak will sink a great ship.

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:15.040
No matter how solid of
an embankment you build,

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:19.250
a small crack can destroy everything.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.080
The one at the top must always be vigilant
of the movements in their periphery.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:31.500
I hope we both live long lives.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:39.160
Well, please take care of this... Minister.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:10.950
"AFTERLOST"

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:15.370
The legendary treasure, Tsuki's Tears,
that sank with a luxury liner in the Pacific

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:16.700
"Episode 5: Affection"
The legendary treasure, Tsuki's Tears,
that sank with a luxury liner in the Pacific

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:20.700
"Episode 5: Affection"
at the beginning of the
19th century, has been found.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:29.200
The discovery was made by an oceanic
research team at Inada University.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:33.290
The large ruby is currently
valued at 500 million yen.

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:35.660
"Hidaka Detective Agency"

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:39.620
Please stop this, sir.

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:46.620
In the middle of the day...

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:52.290
You, too. What happened to your revenge?

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.950
Ryoko's former partner, Aoyama...

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:01.950
...was found as a drowned corpse.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:07.500
The higher-ups have shut down
the investigation division

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.660
and the chief was transferred out.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:17.160
Sir... I'm just as frustrated as you are!

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.660
Please tell me everything you know!

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:26.410
The Agency... Who the hell are they?!

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:31.870
Detective.

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:37.410
Oh. Famous guy.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:38.660
"Hidaka Detective Agency"

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:42.120
"Hidaka Detective Agency"
You wanted 500,000 yen, right?

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:45.830
The other day, the art piece
known as Tsuki's Tears,

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:46.620
--was found in a sunken ship in the Pacific.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.290
--That...
--was found in a sunken ship in the Pacific.

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:49.500
What is it?
--was found in a sunken ship found in the Pacific.

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:52.370
Souma was holding something like that...

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:57.580
If that's the case, that may
have been an Artifact.

00:03:57.580 --> 00:03:59.160
Artifact?

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:00.950
Back when I worked at the research facility,

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:03.870
I had a coworker that
specialized in their research.

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:06.000
Even objects can contain souls.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:10.870
The will of the one who made it, or the will
of the owners throughout the generations.

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:15.910
When such wills condense, there are times
an item will manifest a mysterious power.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:26.620
Why is Souma carrying something like that?

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:32.160
It seems that power can magnify
a human's innate ability.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:36.330
There are rumors that the Agency has been
collecting them from all over the world.

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:40.790
He was sniffing around the mansion.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:44.080
Says he has business with Takuya.
What should we do?

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:49.000
It's the magician, Yoshiaki!

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:58.080
When did you become friends
with such a famous person?

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:01.370
Who told you about me?

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:03.370
I cannot say.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:08.660
This is bad. Doesn't this mean that
someone is looking into Takuya?

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.790
What business do you have with me?

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:15.830
Are you familiar with the
Phantom Thief Brigade X?

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:22.540
I believe you've come into contact
with them a number of times.

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:34.500
Nice try!

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:58.450
You've reminded me of some
really unpleasant memories.

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:01.540
What's your relation to them?

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:05.580
Their leader, Tsubasa... is my older brother.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.250
What did you say?!

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:11.160
I haven't seen him in over 10 years.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:13.870
He suddenly disappeared one day.

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:17.040
And, so?

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:20.950
Will you make a deal with me?

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:29.580
Would someone really go this far
to meet their long-lost brother?

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:34.200
A sibling that leaves their family
behind is just another stranger.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:37.790
Those two lost their parents at an early age.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:41.370
They depended on one another
to survive when they were kids.

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:43.410
I see...

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:47.080
Well, that magician is pretty late.

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:50.540
Could it be that he told them about you, sir?

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:54.290
He's a wuss, but he's not stupid.

00:06:56.830 --> 00:07:00.500
These are the things that the Phantom Thief
Brigade have stolen in the past.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:04.330
They're are all pieces of art worth
hundreds of millions of yen.

00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:07.700
So is their aim money, after all?

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:11.700
There is a jewel called Hoshi's Tears here.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:19.950
The recently recovered Tsuki's Tears is a
legendary treasure that pairs with this item.

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:22.580
I'm sure they will target it.

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:29.660
You're asking me to catch your brother?
What merit is there for us?

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:33.790
Don't you want to recover the stolen
treasures from the Phantom Thief Brigade?

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:38.120
If you catch them, you should be able
to find out how they sell the goods.

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:45.870
This is unfinished business.

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:51.290
Yeah. There's no need to ask the leader.

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:52.830
How are things going?

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:55.250
I'm in the middle of researching it.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:08.160
The Agency has the Hoshi's Tears
that the Phantom Thief Brigade stole.

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:10.830
So they were connected to the Agency?

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:13.830
Takuya, this is a trap.

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:15.040
Yeah.

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:24.450
Sorry. I can't trust someone who won't
tell me the source of their information.

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:27.410
I don't want to do anything rough, but...

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:31.000
Are you sure?

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:33.200
I've told my manager.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:38.370
If something happens to me, he'll tell the
police and the press about this place.

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:40.040
So you're threatening us.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.410
That's a problem.

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:47.370
If I let this chance go by,
I'll never see my brother again...

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:53.040
Um...

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:57.540
Can an Artifact change the
personality of the wielder?

00:08:57.540 --> 00:08:59.830
There is a possibility.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:07.330
If we can examine Tsuki's Tears, maybe we
can find a hint to change Souma back...

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:11.620
Jeez...

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:19.370
Infiltration successful.

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:25.250
Hey. Why is your brother leading the
Phantom Thief Brigade in the first place?

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:27.120
I do not know.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:31.870
After the Lost, he's been quiet.
What has he been doing lately?

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:33.700
I do not know.

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:36.080
As his brother, you should know.

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:41.750
They say it was a traffic accident.

00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:44.160
How terrible.

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:46.790
Her children are still so young.

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:59.540
Father, I'll work hard.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:12.580
You don't have to worry about Souma, either.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.540
How long are we going to tail them?

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:35.660
Who cares about a famous guy like him?

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:43.290
This man named Takuya. He was the
last person she was chasing after.

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:49.330
And in the past, he has been known
to be involved with the Agency.

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:51.370
You should've told me that from the start!

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:03.580
What was that just now?!

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:06.040
Oh, um...

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:09.870
Well, I'm a magician.

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:14.450
Just now...

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:19.290
What do you think about my plan?

00:11:19.290 --> 00:11:24.040
It'd be boring if we just got
a back-up for this thing.

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:28.450
Let's take this chance to
round-up those Artifacts.

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:31.660
We should use that guy, Tsubasa.

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:34.000
I wonder if things will really go that smoothly.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.750
Don't look down on me, old lady.

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:36.910
Old...!

00:11:36.910 --> 00:11:39.500
They'll come, won't they, Suzuna.

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:41.790
Yes. Absolutely.

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:46.160
This girl has already failed once.
We cannot leave things to her.

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:48.120
You, too...

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:50.250
Why not.

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:52.580
Experience is important.

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:56.290
Too bad for you.

00:11:56.290 --> 00:11:58.000
Let's go, Suzuna.

00:11:58.000 --> 00:11:59.410
Yes.

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:07.910
How troublesome.
We should have brainwashed him.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:10.370
He's more interesting this way.

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:13.540
Kids are cute when they're a little cheeky.

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:17.330
I'm the one who gets inconvenienced.

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:21.330
I don't want to be bitten by another pet dog.

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:30.830
What is it?

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:32.370
Nothing.

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:33.870
This is bad...

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:40.040
Found you!

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:41.370
This is bad!

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:45.750
That's dangerous!

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:03.120
What happened?!

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:05.700
We were attacked by someone!

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:10.580
You lose!

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:13.200
We'll be the ones taking Tsuki's Tears.

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:15.450
Have a nice day.

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:17.450
They're playing with us!

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:18.830
Is everyone all right?

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:21.750
Ouch...

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:25.950
I found out where they're keeping Tsuki's Tears.

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:27.580
It's not in their research tower?

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:32.000
No, it looks like they are moving it
to a different place tonight.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:35.080
Tomorrow, a lot of important affiliates
are going to gather to see it.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:39.200
Either way, we can't move forward like this.

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:42.620
My brother is doing something like this...?

00:13:57.160 --> 00:14:01.200
You want to retract our bid?!
No, no. Please don't joke.

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:04.250
Prime real estate like this isn't
easy to come by, you know?

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:08.370
We are making drastic changes
to our business plans.

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:12.620
Are you sure? The penalty
fees will be quite high.

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:15.080
Yes. We do not mind.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:17.500
It will all be gone in the end.

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:18.660
What?

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:26.290
What?!

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:49.080
You failure.

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:53.870
Shit!!

00:15:04.580 --> 00:15:06.370
Tsubasa's data?

00:15:06.370 --> 00:15:10.370
Yes, it was still in the
detective agency's database.

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:14.160
This is the institution he was in as a child.

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:17.910
Light of Hope Academy for the Handicapped...

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:19.790
Then, Yoshiaki, too.

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:21.290
Probably.

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:26.660
That guy... Who put him up to this?

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:39.000
You're crying again, Yoshiaki?

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:41.500
Brother...

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:46.000
Jeez. I guess it can't be helped.
Did you trip over this?

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:51.330
Don't cry. Here. Look.

00:15:57.450 --> 00:16:00.370
Wow! It disappeared!

00:16:00.370 --> 00:16:02.790
Along with your tears!

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:09.080
From Takuya.

00:16:09.080 --> 00:16:10.910
Oh, thank you.

00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:18.410
What kind of person was he?

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:19.370
Huh?

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:21.200
Your brother.

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:22.910
Oh.

00:16:22.910 --> 00:16:27.080
He was a cool big brother.
But he was a strange person.

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:28.700
Strange person?

00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:32.330
For instance. How do you eat fried pork cutlets?

00:16:32.330 --> 00:16:36.910
Huh? How? With sauce, like normal...

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:41.410
My brother takes the breading
off completely before he eats it.

00:16:41.410 --> 00:16:42.290
Huh?

00:16:42.290 --> 00:16:44.000
Strange, right?

00:16:46.410 --> 00:16:51.660
I guess, even as siblings,
there are things you can't understand.

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:54.910
Yeah.

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:10.660
You don't have stay here anymore, Akira.

00:17:10.660 --> 00:17:12.700
Some security officer you turned out to be.

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:15.950
You couldn't protect her.

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:20.580
Don't worry about us and go
stick close to Dad or something!

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:23.120
Your father was the one who ordered me to stay.

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:28.950
Mind your own business!

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:30.790
What's wrong, Souma?!

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:43.040
The Phantom Thief Brigade is definitely here.

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:49.500
Like I thought, those guys are here.

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:53.790
They won't get by with a warning
this time. They just don't learn.

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:56.120
Let's get this over with quickly.

00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:07.200
Are you guys that Phantom Thief Brigade?

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:08.620
A kid?

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:11.290
Kids should be in bed by now!

00:18:11.290 --> 00:18:16.290
Right back at you. Halloween is
already over, Cosplaying Brigade.

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:18.080
What'd you say?!

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:25.500
Why do you have that, in the first place?

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:31.290
Leader!

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:32.700
Oh!

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:37.290
This is!

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:40.580
Just means that we're fine on our own.

00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:45.790
It's fine for you to rest
every once in a while like this.

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:49.830
Sorry. I caused you all trouble.

00:18:49.830 --> 00:18:53.120
But, how did you guys...?

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:55.540
Hm?

00:18:55.540 --> 00:18:57.040
What is it?

00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:01.700
This is a fake...

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:03.750
Huh?!

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:06.950
That means they knew we were after it!

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:09.540
No way...

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:15.540
Well, this is still a pretty nice item!

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:23.370
See? I was thinking this
chandelier was missing something.

00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:32.950
In the end, we never found the real thing.

00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:36.000
Who the hell are you?

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:37.660
Who knows.

00:19:38.950 --> 00:19:43.950
Perfect timing. We'll just steal it
together with Tsuki's Tears.

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:47.200
It'll make our leader happy.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:49.120
Are you guys stupid?

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:50.580
Huh?!

00:19:56.370 --> 00:19:59.870
Tsuki's Tears is gone?

00:19:59.870 --> 00:20:02.660
Did my brother already...?

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:11.830
Souma!

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:14.000
Sis.

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:16.080
That boy?

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:18.700
How lucky to meet you here.

00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:22.540
Thank goodness.
Thank goodness you were all right...

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:28.330
Are you guys his allies?!

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:31.120
Depending on your answer,
we'll finish you off first!

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:33.500
You're all his subordinates, aren't you?!

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:37.160
Why is he holding the
Hoshi's Tears that you stole?!

00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:39.250
We'd like to ask the same question!

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:42.000
Should you all be bickering right now?

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:46.410
Hurry up and tell me where you've hidden
the Artifacts you've stolen until now.

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:50.200
If you don't, she'll die.

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:07.500
Let me tell you.

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:10.620
Adults are scary when you make them angry!

00:21:23.200 --> 00:21:24.500
What?!

00:21:31.330 --> 00:21:33.080
This is so troublesome.

00:21:33.080 --> 00:21:34.700
Stop it...

00:21:34.700 --> 00:21:37.200
Maybe I should just kill all of you now.

00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:39.830
Stop! Souma!

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:42.410
More importantly.

00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:44.700
Why are you still alive?!

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:56.790
I see.

00:22:00.540 --> 00:22:05.330
Long time no see, Akira.

00:23:36.950 --> 00:23:37.950
"AFTERLOST"

00:23:43.910 --> 00:23:46.290
Next Episode: "Parting."
